  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LAND-at-scale Knowledge Management Strategy support (Royal Tropical Institute KIT)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Royal Tropical Institute (KIT) supports the LAND-at-scale (LAS) Knowledge Management strategy. Knowledge Management (KM) is an integral part of the LAND-at-scale programme. The aim of KM is to scale and catalyse the impact of the programme and individual country projects by providing an increased understanding of relevant processes, stakeholders and contexts. KM takes place at programme and country-level; these levels are strongly interlinked. This project serves to implement KM activities at country-level, through the development and (facilitation of) the implementation of country-level KM strategies LAS-countries. In specific, the project facilitates experience capitalisation and outcomes harvesting, to support adaptive programming, qualitative reflection and learning, as well as scaling project impact and lessons learned.</narrative>
  </description>
